    "lab-2026-11-20-physical-reservoir-narma10": {
      "id": "5f0x77m3p7z161ee8674p1yx1r",
      "created": "2026-11-20T23:45:24Z",
      "hash": "sha256:c6c63e752dbaf1c9da3cab63ee21d64fecf984e686cfdea466edfb17576969cb",
      "kind": "thread",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-20-oscillator-reservoir-claim",
          "id": "22v1e3dt4ryr37vxbxcddeevq5",
          "version": 1,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>Toy oscillator reservoir trails tuned ESN on NARMA-10</strong></p>\n<p>In simulation only. A toy network of 50 coupled, noisy oscillators, on the NARMA-10 task at 50 readout features and a 24-configuration grid, reached a median test NMSE of 0.96 over five instances. A tuned echo-state network of the same width reached 0.15. At this grid the toy model sits near mean-predictor level. One task, one toy model, one grid: this says nothing about physical reservoirs in general, or about energy.</p>\n<p>Evidence: experiments/e002-physical-reservoir-narma10/RESULTS.md. Stage: simulated. Review: weakened (wording narrowed to this model, grid and task).</p>\n</div>"
        }
      ],
