    "lab-2026-11-21-chip-native-window-run": {
      "id": "0enta50380qkg47vg4ywwqadvr",
      "created": "2026-11-21T02:29:42Z",
      "hash": "sha256:cdd892a7157a40b05fc9df06cd603d1700f5010e55a61e9152c0265d8f882918",
      "kind": "thread",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-21-chip-native-gap-one-window",
          "id": "3nsrjj02719jqets76w1z0x8p6",
          "version": 1,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>Chip-native nowcaster: 16% of gap on one window</strong></p>\n<p>In simulation, on one rainy 256 × 256 window of a public pysteps radar sequence (seed 1, three forecast origins), a chip-native sampler closed 16% of the CRPS gap between the lab&#39;s naive i.i.d. ensemble and STEPS at 60 minutes. The pre-registered threshold was 50%, so the test was killed. This is one seed and one window, and the naive baseline is the lab&#39;s own construction. It does not test per-scale structure or the published claim, and it is not replicated.</p>\n<p>Evidence: <a href=\"https://github.com/msmsim/kinocomputing-lab/blob/main/experiments/e001-chip-native-nowcast/RESULTS.md\">https://github.com/msmsim/kinocomputing-lab/blob/main/experiments/e001-chip-native-nowcast/RESULTS.md</a></p>\n</div>"
        }
      ],
