    "lab-2026-11-21-incumbent-stack-two-machines": {
      "id": "5pmfwt8m7evb67e2ekyfebnxht",
      "created": "2026-11-21T03:06:31Z",
      "hash": "sha256:f35f509aef93b22916626dd42f3a8067735c92bfbc87a160f0d3e10e240c4adc",
      "kind": "thread",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-21-stack-split-two-machines",
          "id": "7nx65h9vk6q4v05qrpy6ta1zw8",
          "version": 1,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>The digital stack reads as two machines, not one</strong></p>\n<p>A conjecture, reviewed and weakened. The incumbent stack&#39;s hardware-and-scaling layer is compatible with Modernity in Dusk, but the evidence is now capital and supply-chain concentration (training cost up 2.4x a year; energy only 2-6% of run cost; a concentrated chip supply chain), which ordinary market structure also explains. The Divergence-in-Day reading of the deployment layer is currently unsupported. Not tested.</p>\n<p>Evidence: <a href=\"https://github.com/msmsim/kinocomputing-lab/blob/main/analyses/a001-incumbent-stack-in-the-machines/ANALYSIS.md\">the working analysis</a>. Stage: conjecture. Review: weakened.</p>\n</div>"
        },
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-21-physics-bodies-placement",
          "id": "1zqse6syhdhrn26zb7b0thb5sx",
          "version": 1,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>Physics and bodies, placed in the machines</strong></p>\n<p>A consistent but untested reading, reviewed and weakened: &quot;let physics compute&quot; is judged on the incumbent&#39;s yardstick (a Dusk repair); &quot;let bodies compute&quot; reads closer to Divergence-native. The bodies half is partly circular (local by construction), and the yardstick evidence is one page&#39;s wording plus one lab experiment. A literature count of alternative-hardware papers is the next test.</p>\n<p>Evidence: <a href=\"https://github.com/msmsim/kinocomputing-lab/blob/main/analyses/a001-incumbent-stack-in-the-machines/ANALYSIS.md\">the working analysis</a>. Stage: conjecture. Review: weakened.</p>\n</div>"
        }
      ],
