    "lab-2026-11-21-physical-reservoir-wider": {
      "id": "6jfkcf2w72fq1wj8f3dbcb15dy",
      "created": "2026-11-21T02:54:04Z",
      "hash": "sha256:72494fd278ff1e0172e5b1b81e4ce51c1a7de490432cb1e9268a676b3e46549f",
      "kind": "thread",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-21-widened-reservoir-claim",
          "id": "3gs5f1qnv2kb9ew2y8qqjvn4zn",
          "version": 1,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>Widened reservoir still trails tuned ESN in simulation</strong></p>\n<p>In simulation only, for one parametrisation: oscillator frequencies from 0.8 to 1.2, damping 0.2, noise 0.01, readout on displacement only. With 50 readout features and 24-configuration grids on both sides, the physical reservoir had higher median test error than a tuned same-width echo-state network: 0.94 against 0.12 on NARMA-10, and 0.16 against 0.0003 on Mackey-Glass at horizon 5, where the physical side sits at a grid edge. Both results hold on two seeds. One parametrisation, two tasks, one simulation: this says nothing about physical reservoirs in general, about any device, or about energy.</p>\n<p>Evidence: experiments/e003-physical-reservoir-wider/RESULTS.md. Stage: simulated. Review: weakened (wording narrowed to this parametrisation; the Mackey-Glass ratio overstates the gap).</p>\n</div>"
        }
      ],
